{"name":"Banshee","hex":"#daf0e6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"banshee","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female spirit, usually taking the form of a woman whose mournful wailing warns of an impending death.","A noisy or ill-tempered woman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banshee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Banshee","blocks":[{"text":"A banshee is a female spirit in Irish folklore who heralds the death of a family member, usually by screaming, wailing, shrieking, or keening. Her name is connected to the mythologically important tumuli or \"mounds\" that dot the Irish countryside, which are known as síde in Old Irish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Banshee.jpg/330px-Banshee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banshee","wikidata":"Q273112"},{"title":"Banshee (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Banshee is an American action television series created by Jonathan Tropper and David Schickler that aired on Cinemax from January 11, 2013, to May 20, 2016, over four seasons and 38 episodes. Set in the small fictional town of Banshee in Pennsylvania Amish country, the series' main character is an enigmatic ex-con who assumes the identity of Lucas Hood, the town's murdered sheriff, to hide from powerful crime lord Rabbit. Imposing his own brand of justice, Hood attempts to reconcile with his former lover, Rabbit's daughter Anastasia, who has herself adopted an assumed identity, married, and raised a family during Hood's incarceration. Hood struggles to maintain his new identity while still embracing crime alongside his partners Job and Sugar and coming into conflict with local kingpin Kai Proctor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Banshee_%28Home_Box_Office%2C_Inc%29_blood_red_logo.svg/330px-Banshee_%28Home_Box_Office%2C_Inc%29_blood_red_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banshee_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q2813828"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/The_Banshee_Appears_%281862%29.jpg/500px-The_Banshee_Appears_%281862%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/The_Banshee_Appears_%281862%29.jpg/500px-The_Banshee_Appears_%281862%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Banshee Appears, 1862","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Banshee_Appears_(1862).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d7/Banshee_promotional_poster.jpg/250px-Banshee_promotional_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d7/Banshee_promotional_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d7/Banshee_promotional_poster.jpg/250px-Banshee_promotional_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Promotional poster for Banshee","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABanshee_promotional_poster.jpg"}],"sounds":{"banshee":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/67/En-us-banshee.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/67/En-us-banshee.ogg/En-us-banshee.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Flight of three Royal Canadian Navy McDonnell Banshee fighters","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Flight_of_three_Royal_Canadian_Navy_McDonnell_Banshee_fighters.jpg/500px-Flight_of_three_Royal_Canadian_Navy_McDonnell_Banshee_fighters.jpg","ratio":1.328